  "preamble": "Spirantization of the voiced bilabial stop [b] to the voiced bilabial fricative or approximant [β] loosens the lip closure while keeping the bilabial place. In Greek it was a historical change: Attic [b] had become [β] by the Koine period in all positions, before going on to labiodental [v] in Medieval Greek. In Spanish it is a living allophony, in which /b/ is realized as the approximant [β̞] after vowels and most consonants and stays a stop after a pause or a nasal.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Spirantization, Lenition",
